WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.160
Business Email Compromise Training and Awareness: a role-based competency framework for the financial sector.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.740
Financial institutions move billions of dollars every day, on the strength of one thing: trust.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.980
In finance, large payments are routine, and staff are trained to act fast on instructions.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:32.280
Business email compromise turns that trust into a weapon. It rarely looks like an attack.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.380
A criminal pretends to be someone you trust, and asks for something routine, by email.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.280
Then by a cloned voice, one that sounds exactly like someone you know.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.100
Or on a deepfake video call, where even the face looks right.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:08.520
In 2025, people in the United States reported three billion US dollars in losses to the FBI. Worldwide, reported losses passed fifty-five billion.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.360
Add regulator pressure and access to client data, and finance becomes a prime target.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.740
That is why this training is built around six roles, where one decision can move money or data.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.460
Executives.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.200
Accounts payable.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.800
HR and payroll.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.100
Customer service.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.140
IT.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.520
Administration.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:40.360
Every attack pulls the same human levers: Cialdini's six principles of persuasion.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.220
My framework teaches three steps. Detect the attempt.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.160
Verify it somewhere the attacker cannot reach.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.940
And contain the damage if something goes wrong.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:02.940
Learners watch a scenario, spot the red flags in a realistic email, make a decision, and see where they stand.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.280
The impact: one habit, decisions not slides, psychology made visible, and speed when it counts.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.620
Pause. Verify. Report.
